              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "متوتر — mutawattir — \"tense, nervous\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "كانت أختي متوترة قبل المقابلة. kānat ukhtī mutawattira qabla al-muqābala. My sister was nervous before the interview."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The noun توتر, stress, shares the root."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "متوتر (mutawattir) is built on the native Arabic root w-t-r, \"a bowstring\" (Lane). Mutawattir is the participle of Form V: drawn tight, like a bowstring."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
